  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If the script can not run in the requested parcel, this function returns an empty list and issues a warning in the debug channel.</li>
    <li><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/w/index.php?title=SKY_LIGHT&action=edit&redlink=1" target="_blank">SKY_LIGHT</a>'s param <i>fade_color</i> does not return a clamped value, meaning an unusually bright scene will cause it to return an out-of-bounds color. (This can be fixed by clamping the value manually, but this should really return a clamped value).</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local total_number = #events
    local environment = ll.GetEnvironment(ll.GetPos(), {SKY_TRACKS, SKY_AMBIENT, SKY_CLOUDS})
    ll.OwnerSay(ll.DumpList2String(environment, ", "))
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    touch_start(integer total_number)
    {
        list environment = llGetEnvironment(llGetPos(), [SKY_TRACKS, SKY_AMBIENT, SKY_CLOUDS]);
        llOwnerSay(llDumpList2String(environment, ", "));
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
